uped symbolic names enclosed in braces, with a named entry for topology change blocking."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/trace/events/error_report.h::__ERROR_REPORT_DECLARE_TRACE_ENUMS_ONCE_ONLY","include/trace/events/error_report.h::error_detector","include/trace/events/error_report.h::error_detector_list","include/trace/events/error_report.h::EM.alt_1","include/trace/events/error_report.h::EMe.alt_1","include/trace/events/error_report.h::EM.alt_2","include/trace/events/error_report.h::EMe.alt_2","include/trace/events/error_report.h::show_error_detector_list"],"text":"Error reporting distinguishes three detector sources for fence, sanitizer and warning origins, with paired macro forms that first declare enumeration values and then build value to label tables plus a symbolic printer."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/trace/events/huge_memory.h::SCAN_STATUS","include/trace/events/huge_memory.h::EM.alt_1","include/trace/events/huge_memory.h::EMe.alt_1","include/trace/events/huge_memory.h::EM.alt_2","include/trace/events/huge_memory.h::EMe.alt_2"],"text":"Transparent huge page scan tracing uses a large outcome vocabulary that separates success from many distinct failure causes such as unsuitable tables or entries, page state or lifetime problems, virtual area problems, allocation or accounting failures and copy or dirty hazards, with dual macro forms for declaration and table generation."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/trace/events/erofs.h::show_dev","include/trace/events/erofs.h::show_dev_nid","include/trace/events/erofs.h::show_file_type","include/trace/events/erofs.h::show_map_flags","include/trace/events/erofs.h::show_mflags","include/trace/events/ext4.h::show_mballoc_flags","include/trace/events/ext4.h::show_map_flags","include/trace/events/ext4.h::show_mflags","include/trace/events/ext4.h::show_free_flags","include/trace/events/ext4.h::show_extent_status","include/trace/events/ext4.h::show_falloc_mode","include/trace/events/ext4.h::show_fc_reas